<section class="content-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Help centre</span><h1>Find the next step quickly.</h1><p>Guidance for account access, learning, project work and platform administration.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container help-layout"><nav class="panel help-nav" aria-label="Help topics"><span class="eyebrow">Topics</span><a href="#accounts">Accounts and access</a><a href="#learning">Learning and assessment</a><a href="#projects">Code Lab and projects</a><a href="#staff">Teacher and administrator operations</a><a href="#installation">Installation</a></nav><div class="faq-stack"><section id="accounts"><span class="eyebrow">Accounts and access</span><details open><summary>How do I create a learner account?</summary><p>Open the registration page, provide a unique username and email address, select an age group and create a strong password. Registration is available only when an administrator has enabled it.</p></details><details><summary>Can I sign in with my username?</summary><p>Yes. The sign-in form accepts either the registered username or email address. Repeated failed attempts are temporarily limited to protect accounts.</p></details><details><summary>What happens when an account is disabled?</summary><p>The user can no longer sign in. An administrator can restore access from User Management without deleting the learner's progress or projects.</p></details></section><section id="learning"><span class="eyebrow">Learning and assessment</span><details><summary>How do I begin a course?</summary><p>Open Learning Paths, review the outcomes and enrol. The course page then shows the ordered lesson sequence and your saved completion status.</p></details><details><summary>How is a lesson completed?</summary><p>Read the lesson, complete its practical challenge and submit the quiz. A score of at least 60% marks the lesson complete; lower scores remain recorded so the learner can improve.</p></details><details><summary>Where does quiz feedback come from?</summary><p>Every question, answer and explanation is stored in the curriculum database and maintained by administrators. The platform calculates the score from those records.</p></details></section><section id="projects"><span class="eyebrow">Code Lab and projects</span><details><summary>How does MwanaCode run safely?</summary><p>Code Lab recognises a defined set of learning commands and enforces execution limits. It does not use JavaScript eval() and cannot run arbitrary browser scripts.</p></details><details><summary>Does saving overwrite my work?</summary><p>Saving updates the project and records a new version when the code changes. Previous versions remain available in the database for audit and recovery.</p></details></section><section id="staff"><span class="eyebrow">Staff operations</span><details><summary>What can teachers see?</summary><p>Teachers can review learner participation, course completion, quiz performance and individual learner reports. They cannot change platform administration settings.</p></details><details><summary>What can administrators manage?</summary><p>Administrators manage accounts, roles, status, learning paths, lessons, quiz questions, announcements, public branding and operational settings.</p></details></section><section id="installation"><span class="eyebrow">Installation</span><details><summary>Can CodeMwana run on XAMPP?</summary><p>Yes. Copy the project to htdocs, create the database, configure .env and open setup.php. The installer creates the schema, curriculum and first administrator account from the information entered during installation.</p></details></section></div></div></section>
